Evolve an expression fitting a CSV of expected values

<BIN> run [OPTIONS]

OPTIONS:
  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit
          --data TEXT:FILE REQUIRED 
                              CSV data points: header row of variable names, last column
                              'expected'
          --epochs UINT [50]  Epochs to evolve
          --seed UINT [0]     Random seed (0 = nondeterministic)
          --max-population UINT [100000]  
                              World size
          --tournament-size UINT [3]  
                              Tournament selection size
          --population-decrease FLOAT [0.9]  
                              Survivor share kept between epochs
          --operators TEXT [+-*/^]  
                              Binary operators available to mutation
          --scalar-range FLOAT [5]  
                              Random constants are drawn from [-range, range]
          --expression TEXT ... 
                              Initial expression, repeatable (replaces the config list)
          --random-count UINT [200]  
                              Random organisms seeded into the initial population
          --random-depth UINT [4]  
                              Max tree depth of the random initial organisms
          --print-top UINT [10]  
                              World rows to print (0 = all)
          --print-every UINT [10]  
                              Print the world every N epochs (0 = only start and final)

Config:
          --config TEXT:FILE  Load settings from a JSON file (as written by --save-config);
                              flags below override individual fields from the loaded config.
          --save-config TEXT  Write the effective config JSON to this path
